

                                 File Menu Help
                                 --------------


The file area is for sending and receiving files to and from the BBS.


A - Area Change

    Lets you change to a specific file area.

D - Download File

    Lets you receive a file from the BBS using your selected protocal.
    Keep in mind your upload:download ratio, i.e for every so many
    downloads, you must upload a file.  The file may be in any area.

G - Good-Bye

    When you want to logoff of the board, use this command.  DO NOT DROP
    CARRIER OR YOUR ACCESS WILL BE LOWERED.

K - Kill a File

    This will delete a file in the current area from the drive.  Only those
    with SysOp access can use this command.

F - File Listing

    This will give a listing of all available files for downloading in the
    current area.

B - Browse Mode Toggle

    Toggles between Browse Mode and Normal Listing Mode.  With browse mode
    on, files are listed one at a time with all information being
    displayed, instead of one file per line.

C - Clear Marked List

    "Unmarks" all the files that you have marked.

N - New Files

    This command allows you to search for new files since your last logon,
    or since any date you specify.  You will be given the option of
    searching all areas, or just the current one.

Q - Quit to Main Menu

    This takes you back to the Main Menu of the BBS.

S - Search File List

    This searches the file listing for a filename or description that
    contains the string you specify.  You will be given the option of
    searching all areas, or just the current one.

U - Upload File

    This command allows you to send a file to the BBS.  After the transfer,
    you will be prompted for a description.  Please be precise as possible
    in your description, do not enter things like "Neat awesome game",
    instead do something more like "Space Invaders Clone, very good.".

V - View Archive Contents

    Most files available for download are stored in archives, which allows
    for many files to be stored in one compressed file.  To get a listing
    of what's inside an archive, use this command.  Be aware that there are
    numerous archiving formats and only some are supported by this BBS. 
    The file can be from any available area.

E - Entire File Listing

    This will list the files available for downloading in all available
    file areas.

R - Read Text File

    If there is a text file in the files section that is not archived, and
    you'd like to read it but not download it, then use this command.  The
    file can be from any available area.

I - Information on File

    To get a little more info on a file than is displayed in the file
    listing, use this command.  It will display the file size, description,
    who uploaded it, time to download, etc.

